| riscos-mesa OpenAL test: double-click to run. Plays three tones (middle,
| left, right) through OpenAL and SDL's sound driver and saves the results
| in "altone" in this directory. It has no window: it takes about 4 seconds.
Dir <Obey$Dir>
| OpenAL mixes in SDL's audio thread: load UnixLib's PThreadTicker module
| (PThrTicker, here) first, which keeps the thread switcher safe in the
| desktop.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad PThrTicker
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
Run altest -o altone
